{"verdict": "insufficient",
  "answer": "No evidence was retrieved, and a direct search of the corpus (13 KBs, incl. KB-SciFact 148 docs) finds no document containing \"DIF2\" and none reporting that RA activation in NB4 cells induces hallmarks of transcriptionally active promoters. The only NB4/RA document found ([24624992]) shows RA rapidly induces IEX-1 in NB4/KG1 cells via two functional RA-response elements in the IEX-1 promoter — promoter-level activation, but not active-promoter chromatin hallmarks and nothing about DIF2. The other promoter-related document ([13639330]) concerns ligand-dependent promoter gating by histone methyltransferases/demethylases (LSD1) and does not mention NB4 cells or DIF2. The claim therefore cannot be verified from the corpus.",
  "evidence_used": ["24624992", "13639330"]}
